.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-complexity 1  "complexity " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-complexity \- What the analyser measured, as a distribution rather than only its tail
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx complexity\fR [\fB\-\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-min\fR] [\fB\-\-histogram\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
What the analyser measured, as a distribution rather than only its tail
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
relaxed, standard, strict or pristine
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fI<BY>\fR [default: function]
One row per function, per file, or per directory
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
function
.IP \(bu 2
file
.IP \(bu 2
dir
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<SORT>\fR [default: complexity]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
complexity
.IP \(bu 2
statements
.IP \(bu 2
nesting
.IP \(bu 2
params
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI<TOP>\fR [default: 20]
How many rows
.TP
\fB\-\-min\fR \fI<MIN>\fR [default: 0]
Skip anything below this, on whatever `\-\-sort` measures
.TP
\fB\-\-histogram\fR
Draw the distribution as well as the worst of it
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit one JSON object per row
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads. Defaults to the machine\*(Aqs parallelism
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file, layered over any `rqx.yaml` found
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Never open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rqx complexity \-\-top 20             the twenty worst functions
  rqx complexity \-\-by dir             the worst of each directory
  rqx complexity \-\-histogram          where the codebase actually sits
